{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.835323Z","id":"9af25a7800d328f862b2b6ab15b464b9df4a9d480e1aa4459bee94116ed620d2","body":{"detail":"path p export codex|pi|copilot records the caller's cwd (std::env::current_dir) as the session's instead of the source session's; the hermetic tool ran from / and this constant stands in for that. When the export is fixed to carry the source cwd, known_defects@claude.snap changes (written_cwd becomes the source cwd) and this constant becomes unused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"The pipeline hands codex, pi and copilot projectors the hermetic caller cwd `/`, which is what a fixed caller-cwd defect would stop writing","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.846593Z","id":"2a4e07671b0f5bf4860a70cbf11abaa0b0eba48650bdcc83d254467fe141f52d","body":{"detail":"The other three agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, drop the canonical form here so the golden is the real bytes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.856774Z","id":"8cb0124a31291ac6b5706d40348239520356a7341a7ba8604e38ff84b8e6ced9","body":{"detail":"round_trip@copilot@claude.snap is now 'compared' where goldens/roundtrip/copilot-claude.json pinned an error from the hermetic placement step (fixture lacks the session identity claude needs). The Unreadable variant stays for a future pair that genuinely cannot be re-read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":281},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"b7b8e0322b119b1e986444e6d40af469ad399cce43b194183a3e3a07d276fb11"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.866880Z","id":"e185bc72fd107804a11a04224fadc4672443192143435772c4cf6f53c3bc8a3a","body":{"detail":"The old tool's judge functions (Fixed vs Worse) classified a changed body; here the classification is the reviewer's, guided by tests/goldens.rs's doc comment. Resolve this record when a defect is fixed and its snapshot accepted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"2e1040b296bb70b5e4614fe3f886af2ddb83174dab983c22fda92737fc98ffe0"},"summary":"Three defects pinned as expected current behaviour; a diff in known_defects@<set>.snap is FIXED or WORSE and must be read, insta cannot tell the two apart","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
